From: Couch <couch@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] Show a background picture until the first window maps

Cage draws black from the moment it takes the screen until a client draws, and its first
frame on a new output is an empty buffer (black) even when a client is already connected.
On a TV that boots into a splash, that's a black blink between the boot splash and the
first window.

-b FILE loads an uncompressed 24-bit TGA into the bottom of the scene: centred, the rest of
the output filled with its top-left pixel, as the Raspberry Pi kernel draws its fullscreen
logo. A new output's first frame is drawn from the scene (as output_config_apply already
does), so the modeset shows the picture, not black. The background is removed when the
first window maps, so after that Cage draws exactly as without it.

For Couch (https://github.com/alecschoen/couch), on top of Raspberry Pi OS's cage 0.3.1.
